* ''Critical procedures take a confirm gate'' (operator, 2026-11-13: //"Note for the future (find the DreamNet/DreamDom roadmaps and survey then true up and add) that critical procedures like `lares("vessel", "reset")` and its UX twin should get gated behind an operator/user confirmation (like the pwd, etc)."//). A critical procedure and its page twin stand behind a confirmation of the operator or user who holds the device. The browser's `lares("vessel", "reset")` and the page's own button raise one reset ask, and the ceremony document burns the place only on the pass its confirm gate mints (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/browser-vessel-lift#/the-confirm-gate`>>; `C4` in #/the-leaps). The host shim's `reset` takes a typed word alone (`C10`). The gate's shape rests in the house's lean below, overrulable (#/open).

